@startuml
' Purpose: Research consent lifecycle states
' Source of truth:
'   src/api/schemas/journey.ts
'   src/api/service/researchConsents.ts

title Research Consent Lifecycle - State Diagram

state "GRANTED\n(active)" as GRANTED
state "REVOKED\n(withdrawn, terminal)" as REVOKED
state "DECLINED\n(terminal)" as DECLINED

[*] --> GRANTED : grantConsent(\n  patientId,\n  researchModuleId,\n  patientJourneyId,\n  grantedByUserId\n)\ngrantedAt = now()

[*] --> DECLINED : declineConsent(\n  patientId, researchModuleId,\n  patientJourneyId, userId, reason?\n)\n(no active consent)\ngrantedAt = revokedAt = now()

GRANTED --> REVOKED : revokeConsent(\n  consentId,\n  revokedByUserId,\n  reason?\n)\n or declineConsent (active consent)\nrevokedAt = now()

REVOKED --> [*]
DECLINED --> [*]

note right of GRANTED
  Idempotency:
  If an active Consent already exists
  for the same (patientId, researchModuleId,
  patientJourneyId), grantConsent returns
  the existing record without creating
  a duplicate.
end note

note right of REVOKED
  The record is NEVER deleted.
  revokedAt, revokedByUserId and optional
  withdrawalReason are set for audit
  purposes (GCP ICH E6).
  hasActiveConsent() returns false.

  A new call to grantConsent
  after revocation creates a
  fresh Consent record.
  Both the revoked and the new
  record are preserved in
  AppState.researchConsents.
end note

note right of DECLINED
  A decline is recorded as a Consent with
  revokedAt equal to grantedAt, which
  distinguishes it from a post-consent
  withdrawal.
end note

note bottom
  Service: src/api/service/researchConsents.ts
  Storage: AppState.researchConsents[]
  UI: src/components/journey/ConsentDialog/ (Grant, Decline),
      src/components/journey/RevokeConsentDialog.tsx
end note

@enduml
